## 1. Purpose and scope

BIFp2p supports direct Bitcoin exchange, financial freedom, and responsible
cooperation within the Bitcoin community. Source access is offered to help
others inspect, improve, translate and independently operate the software,
subject to the conditions below.

In the spirit of humility and service associated with Satoshi Nakamoto's
contribution to Bitcoin, we do not consider ourselves greater or more
important than Bitcoin's creator. We ask operators to honour the work of
others and help sustain tools that benefit the community. This is the
project's ethical position, not a quotation from Satoshi, a claim about
Satoshi's personal obligations, or an endorsement by Satoshi.

These terms are license conditions, not merely an optional donation request.
Their ethical purpose does not make attribution or royalty payment optional.
No guarantee of legal enforceability or successful collection is made.

"Software" means the original BIFp2p code and accompanying material supplied
under this license, including covered portions in modified or renamed versions.
Third-party dependencies remain under their own licenses.

"Operator" means a person or entity operating the Software to facilitate
actual Bitcoin trades, whether or not the deployment is described as
commercial, nonprofit, free, private or community-run.

## 2. Permission

Subject to compliance with this license, you may inspect, use, copy, modify,
translate and redistribute the Software, and operate an independent deployment.

Retain this license, existing copyright notices and the original attribution.
Distributed modified versions must identify material changes, distinguish their
maintainer from Paul, and preserve these terms for the covered Software.
You may license your independently authored additions separately only where
doing so does not remove these conditions from the covered Software.

Offline development, review and simulated tests without actual trades do not
generate trade royalties. Live trades are not exempt merely because a
deployment is labelled a test.

This is a custom source-available license, not an OSI-approved open-source license.

